    "assumptions": [
      "Noncritical TCP/IP, TLS and BLE code executes from mapped Flash after linker/cache-off contract changes.",
      "Bulk network, TLS and BLE allocations may use PSRAM only where port and access lifetime permit.",
      "Internal DMA 48KiB covers display, audio, SD and C6 including descriptors and alignment. It may shrink to 32KiB after concurrent measurements, returning 16KiB to heap.",
      "Stack, DMA, static control and dynamic heap allocations must be charged to exactly one parent.",
      "64KiB internal free reserve remains at the combined standard-workload peak; largest free block also gates admission.",
      "C6 RAM is separate and unavailable to the P4 allocator.",
      "Current two-owner PSRAM heaps must be replaced or coordinated by an admission broker; global sum alone does not prove admission.",
      "VM remains charged at 8MiB for a 4MiB payload until external-metadata leases are integrated and qualified.",
      "Filesystem and SQLite WAL caches are included in their 2MiB service envelopes.",
      "Additional app code must fit a reviewed Flash partition; current native app 775744B leaves 272832B in the 1MiB partition.",
      "IME gets 2MiB of charged PSRAM backing and 8KiB internal control from existing kernel allowance; shares the input task.",
      "Full dictionary and font payloads remain on Flash/SD, with bounded read caches and a built-in fallback dictionary.",
      "The IME two-MiB envelope requires a reader interface instead of the MeOS contiguous dictionary pointer API.",
      "PSRAM batches may be 32KiB but initial internal SD DMA commands are at most 16KiB to fit the staging allowance."
    ],
